lation.</p>'}</div></div><div class="progressive"><details><summary>See the exact calculation</summary><div class="details-body"><p>At weight w=${state.weight}, each factor below multiplies ζ(w):</p><div class="scroll-math">Root permutation: ${esc(m.root_factor)}<br>Reflection spectrum: ${esc(m.reflection_factor)}<br>Combined: ${esc(m.combined_factor)}</div><p>The exact combined coefficient of π<sup>${state.weight}</sup> is:</p><div class="exact-fraction">${esc(m.combined_pi)}</div><p>The two factors come from 8 × 30<sup>1−w</sup> and (2<sup>1−w</sup>−1)(3<sup>1−w</sup>−1)(5<sup>1−w</sup>−1). Standard even-zeta values then supply the π power.</p><p>${validity('Re(w)>1 · normalized Mellin integral')}</p></div></details><details><summary>What does the E8 picture show?</summary><div class="details-body"><p>It is an orbit diagram: eight rings, each containing 30 actual root-permutation positions. Moving one step around every ring represents the Coxeter action. It is not a geometric projection of the eight-dimensional roots.</p><p>The reflection eigenphases are 1, 7, 11, 13, 17, 19, 23 and 29 out of 30. Raising the original q phase to the 56th power reaches the 30th-root phase. The 384-dimensional cyclotomic model restricts to 48 copies of the eight-dimensional Coxeter module.</p><p>${adjointVerified?'The retained Chevalley/Tits construction checks the actual root-space signs, the complete Jacobi sweep, and bracket preservation for all eight simple lifts. Its eight root cycles each have positive total sign, giving the displayed adjoint spectrum.':'The displayed 248-dimensional combination is a verified cyclic direct sum. This retained baseline receipt does not establish an adjoint-lift identification.'} Neither construction establishes the supplied artifacts’ categorical unification.</p></div></details></div>`);
